WEBVTT

00:01:25.996 --> 00:01:30.396
The most anomalous extreme event
since records began 200 years ago

00:01:30.396 --> 00:01:33.476
was in the Pacific Northwest
of North America.

00:01:33.516 --> 00:01:35.116
Forty nine and a half degrees,

00:01:35.156 --> 00:01:39.516
121 degrees Fahrenheit
in British Columbia.

00:01:39.556 --> 00:01:41.956
In the tropics and subtropics,

00:01:41.996 --> 00:01:44.796
the combination
of temperature and humidity

00:01:44.796 --> 00:01:49.116
is now making larger
areas literally uninhabitable,

00:01:49.156 --> 00:01:52.956
the area so described
is relatively small now,

00:01:52.996 --> 00:01:55.996
but if we continue
over the next few decades,

00:01:56.036 --> 00:01:58.796
these areas are predicted to expand,

00:01:58.836 --> 00:02:05.476
and billions of people will be in areas
where it is not safe to stay outside